  "id": "COMPOUND:15192 - PROTEIN:5944",
  "verbalization": "Isoorientin 4'-O-glucoside is implicated in the biological pathway leading to Mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase 8 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that the compound acts as a target for a metabolite, which in turn is a target of another compound, Cycloeudesmol. This indicates a chain of molecular targets that ultimately converge on the kinase kinase kinase 8. The presence of multiple metabolites as intermediates highlights the complexity of the pathway, with Isoorientin 4'-O-glucoside serving as a central node in the network. The integration of these pathways underscores the role of these metabolites in modulating the activity of the kinase, potentially through indirect mechanisms. The evidence supports a mechanism where the compound influences the activity of the kinase through a series of intermediate targets, though the exact nature of the interactions remains to be fully elucidated.",
